{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Recipe",
  "recipeCuisine": "United Kingdom",
  "name": "Arbroath Smokie Kedgeree With Grilled Haddock & Grain Mustard Cream Sauce",
  "text": "Arbroath Smokie Kedgeree With Grilled Haddock & Grain Mustard Cream Sauce\n\nPreparation time:\n\nCooking time:\n\nYield:\n\nIngredients\n\n1 onion (diced),\n\n1 tsp garlic purée,\n\n250g butter,\n\n1kg Arborio rice,\n\n500ml white wine,\n\n2l fish stock,\n\n250g Parmesan (grated),\n\n200ml cream,\n\n2 flaked Arbroath Smokies 1 pkt,\n\ndill (finely chopped),\n\nSalt and pepper.\n\nFor the grain mustard sauce\n\n570ml cream\n\n570ml fish stock,\n\n2 tbsp coarse grain mustard,\n\nJuice of 1 lemon,\n\nSalt and pepper\n\nPreparation\n\n1. Sweat onion and garlic in half the butter. • Add rice and sweat for 2 minutes. • Add wine and stock bit by bit.\n\n2. Bring to boil, reduce heat.\n\n3. Simmer for 15 minutes or so, until liquid is absorbed and rice is cooked.\n\n4. Add flaked Smokies, then add rest of butter, cream, Parmesan and dill.\n\n5. Stir until all combined and butter melted.\n\n6. Season to taste.\n\nFor the sauce\n\n7. Place cream, stock, lemon juice and mustard in pan.\n\n8. Bring to boil and reduce until coats the back of a spoon, season to taste.\n\nFor The Haddock\n\n9. Place portion of haddock on tray, season with salt, drizzle with fresh squeezed lemon juice, place knob of butter on top. Grill until just cooked.\n\n10. Assembly\n\n11. Spoon kedgeree onto centre of plate, place grilled haddock on top, top with soft poached egg and drizzle mustard cream sauce over the top and around plate.",
  "recipeIngredient": [
    "1 onion (diced),",
    "1 tsp garlic purée,",
    "250g butter,",
    "1kg Arborio rice,",
    "500ml white wine,",
    "2l fish stock,",
